  <content>
  <section><section class="check-understanding"><title>Cool Down Activity</title><exercise id="_650e2f67-e71c-4963-8f3e-5322c96c2458" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>1. Which of these polynomials has a greatest common factor of 1?</para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(10q^2 + 14q + 20\)</para><para>\(12x^3 − 2x\)</para><para>\(12x^3y − 7g^8h^3 + 11s^2\)</para><para>\(-2x-4\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \(12x^3y − 7g^8h^3 + 11s^2\)</para><para>Try again. Check to see if \(2\) is a factor in each term in the expression.</para></solution></exercise></section><para>Determine if the expression can be factored by grouping. If it can, factor the expression. If not, answer “prime.”</para>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>\(cd + 6c + 4d + 24\)</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
